[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000]   Good morning, ladies and gentlemen, and welcome to the Monroe, Inc. Earnings Conference Call for the third quarter Fiscal 2020.
[00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000]   At this time, all participants are on a listen only mode.
[00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000]   Later, we will conduct a question and answer session, and instructions will follow at that time.
[00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000]   If anyone should require assistance during the call, please press *0 on your touch-tone phone.
[00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000]   As a reminder, ladies and gentlemen, this conference is being recorded and may not be reproduced in whole or in part without permission from the company.
[00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000]   I would now like to introduce Ms. Maureen Mulholland, Senior Vice President, General Counsel, and Secretary of Monroe.
[00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000]   Thank you. Please go ahead.
[00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000]   Thank you. Hello, everyone, and thank you for joining us on this morning's call.
[00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:53.000]   Before we get started, please note that as part of the call this morning, we will be referencing a presentation that is available on the investors section of our website at
[00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000]   corporate.munroe.com/investors
[00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.000]   resources.
[00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:16.000]   If I could draw your attention to the Safe Harbor Statement on slide 2 of the presentation, I'd like to remind participants on this morning's call that our presentation includes some forward-looking statements about Monroe's future performance.
[00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.000]   Actual results may differ materially from those suggested by our comments today.
[00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.000]   The most significant factors that could affect future results are outlined in Monroe's filings with the SEC,
[00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000]   and in our earnings release.
[00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:43.000]   The company disclaims any intention or obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statements, whether as a result of new information, future events, or otherwise, except as required by law.
[00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:56.000]   Additionally, on today's call, management statements include a discussion of certain non-GAAP financial measures, which are intended to supplement and not be substituted for comparable GAAP measures.
[00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:06.000]   Reconciliations of such supplementalmental information to the comparable GAAP measures will be included as part of today's presentation and in our earnings release.
[00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000]   With that, I'd like to turn the call over to our President and Chief Executive Officer, Brett Pontin.
[00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.000]   Brett?
[00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000]   Thank you, Maureen, and good morning, everyone.
[00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000]   Thanks for joining us.
[00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:25.000]   I'll get started today with a brief overview of our third quarter results, followed by an update on the progress we've made on our Monroe forward strategy.
[00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:38.000]   As illustrated on slide 3, we reported comps down 0.9% in the third quarter as higher year-over-year ticket was offset by negative traffic.
[00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000]   In October and the beginning of November, we performed well against difficult comparisons in the prior year.
[00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:52.000]   Mild weather conditions toward the end of November and end of December caused a slow down across our core northern markets.
[00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.000]   These conditions have continued into January with our comparable stories.
[00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.000]   With our comparable store sales down 4% during the month.
[00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:06.000]   We do not like talking about the weather, however, it is impossible to ignore the impact it has on our business.
[00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:14.000]   While we are not satisfied with our financial results this quarter, we are executing well against the areas within our control.
[00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:21.000]   In particular, we continue to move deeper into our company transformation and are confident we are on the right path.
[00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.000]   We are committed to making the necessary changes
[00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:32.000]   across our organization to position us to deliver strong results no matter the external circumstances.
[00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:41.000]   Moving on to our performance by category in the third quarter, we were down 1% year-over-year in tire comparable store sales.
[00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.000]   As higher ticket, year-over-year was offset by a decline in tire volume.
[00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:53.000]   We experienced more normalized retail price in this quarter and our focus on further refining our tire strategy
[00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000]   to drive strength in our largest category.
[00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:04.000]   Importantly, we are on track to roll out our tire category management and pricing system beginning in the first quarter of fiscal 2021.
[00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.000]   Which will enable a more dynamic and sophisticated approach to real-time pricing.
[00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.000]   I'll provide more details on this shortly.
[00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.000]   Turning to our service and repair categories, we saw a 3% decline in breaks year-over-year.
[00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.000]   Falling short of a difficult comparison in the third quarter last year.
[00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:29.000]   In maintenance, we were flat while front-end shocks were down 1% and alignments declined 3% year-over-year.
[00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:38.000]   Overall, our southern markets outperformed our northern markets as expected given the mild winter weather conditions we faced in this region.
[00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:46.000]   New stores added $22.7 million in revenue during the quarter, including $20.7 million from recent acquisitions.
[00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.000]   Regarding our gross margin performance during the quarter, we saw a decline of 20 basis points
[00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:57.000]   compared to the prior year period, primarily driven by the decrease in our comparable store sales,
[00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000]   which resulted in higher fixed costs as a percentage of sales.
[00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:08.000]   Our variable margin, on the other hand, expanded due to lower year-over-year material costs as a percentage of sales.
[00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:15.000]   While slightly higher than the prior year quarter, technician labor as a percentage of sales decreased sequentially from last quarter.
[00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.000]   This is a good example of us executing well against the areas within our control.
[00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:27.000]   We identified issues last quarter that arose from our transformation and took corrective action to drive improved results.
[00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.000]   We will have additional opportunities to continue to improve results in this area
[00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:38.000]   as we implement our cloud-based source staffing and scheduling model towards the end of this fiscal year,
[00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:46.000]   which will be critical for us to seamlessly adjust the changes and demand dynamics without sacrifice and sales.
